# GLM-5.3-Flash (Z.ai, August 2026): 320B MoE, 18B active, trained to a 1M window.
# 34 of its 45 layers use linear attention and the rest sparse attention over a
# compressed cache, so a long window costs little memory. The release weights are
# 328 GB; this is Unsloth's 2-bit build, the largest that leaves room for the cache.
# 2026-10-15: the fit gave it a 497,920 window with 3 GB of memory left. It answered at
# 70k (3/3, 19 tok/s, tools and thinking fine), then 61% into a 144k prompt the GPU
# driver's allocations started failing and the Spark hung. Something in the long prompt
# needs memory the fit does not count. Any smaller window or bigger margin is a guess
# until the memory is watched through one prompt of each size.
TITLE="GLM-5.3-Flash"
DETAIL="320B, 18B active, 2-bit GGUF, 102 GB"
HF_REPO=unsloth/GLM-5.3-Flash-GGUF
HF_INCLUDE="*UD-IQ2_XXS*"
GGUF_MATCH="UD-IQ2_XXS"
ALIAS=glm-5.3-flash
CTX=fit                     # start from the trained 1M and shrink only if it does not fit
CTX_MIN=262144
KV_TYPE=f16
MIN_FREE_GB=100
EXTRA_ARGS="--load-mode dio --cache-ram 0 --timeout 14400 --reasoning on --reasoning-format auto"
